{
  "id": "perceptual-classification",
  "term": "perceptual classification",
  "definition": "Perceptual classification is the grouping of sounds into types based on how people hear and distinguish them. In this study, it refers to the human-judged sorting of eastern quoll vocalisations, which was then compared with statistical analyses to see how well the perceived categories matched objective patterns.",
